Description: scope stack ordering to branches of the stack's own repository
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

Stack edges were matched on bare branch name. gh answers --head and --base by
name alone, so a fork pull request whose head branch shared a name with a real
stack member was joined into the ordering as a sibling, and the watcher then
drove a pull request nobody in this repository could merge as if it were part of
the stack. The listing now reads headRepository and headRepositoryOwner and only
a pull request whose head branch lives in the repository the stack belongs to
takes part in the ordering.

